d innovations Cooperation with HEI and research institutes Collaboration with cities and regions Support us News and events Highlights News Events Aalto University Magazine OurBlogs Podcasts About us About Aalto University Our strategy Sustainability Code of Conduct Aalto Handbook Campus People and contact information For the media Careers Tools and services All tools (requires login) All services Most used tools Aalto AI Assistant Abacus-accounting Abacus-planning Asio (booking.aalto.fi) Halli Marketing Cloud MOT Kielipalvelu (language service) Neo People hub Phone book PowerBI report finder Salesforce (Service platform) Tiima Webmail Webropol Workday Most used services AI in Aalto Communications services HR services IT Services Learning services Occupational health Research and innovation services Teacher's Handbook Travel services For students Sisu MyCourses MyStudies Browse all courses Safety and emergencies Emergencies Safety and security observations Cyber Security Cyber Security incident report Other Aalto Space Aalto University Shop Brand library and design system Lunch menus EN FI SV Apply to Aalto Donate Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Log in Search Open positions University Teacher or University Lecturer in Design and Manufacturing Technology 11.9.2026 Application closes on 22.10.2026 Unit School of Arts, Design and Architecture Job category Other teaching and research personnel Aalto University is where science and art meet technology and business. We shape a sustainable future by making research breakthroughs in and across our disciplines, sparking the game changers of tomorrow and creating novel solutions to major global challenges. Our community is made up of 16 000 students and 5 200 employees, including 446 professors. Our campus is in Espoo, Greater Helsinki, Finland.  Diversity is part of who we are, and we actively work to ensure our community’s diversity and inclusiveness. This is why we warmly encourage qualified candidates from all backgrounds to join our community. The Aalto School of Arts, Design and Architecture (ARTS) is a Nordic leader in higher education for design, fashion, games, media, architecture, film, art education and fine art. We produce world-class research e.g. in design, digital media and visual culture, art education, urban planning and architecture. Our graduates innovate in and beyond their fields, drawing on over a century of tradition of our institution, a humane and forward-looking approach, and the latest technologies. The Department of Design is a diverse community of competent, creative and responsible individuals. In design, we appreciate technical skill, social significance and artistic expression. The department educates front-line design professionals and visionaries for established, changing and emerging fields of design. We renew our expertise through high level research in continuous collaboration with our stakeholders and partners. We strive towards a sustainable and just society and environment. Faculty consists of 20 lecturers and 20 professors. Our close to 800 students can study product, service and experimental design, textile and fashion design, co-design, design leadership, design research and sustainable development towards Bachelor’s, Master’s and Doctor’s degrees. The Department of Design is looking for University Teacher or University Lecturer in Design and Manufacturing Technology Who has rich practical experience of manufacturing designs in an industrial context and strong interest in educating future designers. Your role and goals In this position, you are responsible for educating students in turning design concepts into such prototypes that can be industrially manufactured with both mature and emerging technologies, including Manufacturing techniques relevant to product design (such as the design and mechanical engineering of an injection-moulded plastic product to be ready for production) CAD and CAM software in an industrial context Basics of prototyping including model making In addition to teaching, duties typically include participating in the development of teaching, design activities and research at the Department of Design. You will participate in the guidance and assessment of student assignments and theses and take part in the intake of new students when needed. Your network and team You will be mainly working with The Department of Design lecturers and professors Bachelor’s Programme in Design and Fashion students majoring in design. Language of the Programme is Finnish and Swedish but teaching is possible also in English Bachelor’s Programme in Design and Media students. Language of the Programme is English Master’s Programme in Design students. Language of the Programme is English, Finnish and Swedish Workshop masters University administrative staff Your experience and ambitions The ideal candidate for this position has rich experience communicating with designers, understanding design intents, and seeing them towards realization. is interested in bridging industrial practices with design education (e.g., bringing design projects and industrial partners into courses) can teach industrial manufacturing processes for scaled production as well as some one-off prototyping skills is able to apply digital fabrication knowledge in collaboration with digital modelling teachers has experience on curriculum design and development of teaching Requirements for this position are Master’s degree in design or relevant field Documented track record in design practice, in industry or manufacturing contexts Strong interest in teaching design students in practical skills as well as guiding theses Proficiency in English The following are considered as advantages Experience in University level teaching Proficiency in Finnish and/or Swedish Research and other merits relevant to the field of the lectureship Documented pedagogic training What we offer We offer you a responsible and meaningful role with true impact in the Department of Design’s success, and in the wellbeing and development of the society. You have the opportunity of working in a dynamic world-class community of creative professionals and researchers, who are committed to exploring the frontiers of design practice and research. For hands-on projects, we have well-equipped workshops (3D printing, laser cutter, mechatronics, solid materials, ceramics, glass, etc.) for building prototypes from different materials. Aalto University’s vast array of professional development opportunities means you will grow and learn, having the chance to participate actively in staff trainings and development projects based on your interests and needs. We value work-life balance and wellbeing in all aspects of life. We work in a hybrid model, with the primary workplace located at the Otaniemi Campus in Espoo, Finland. Life on the revitalized campus is vibrant, featuring stunning architecture, tranquil nature, and a variety of cafes, restaurants, and services, all complemented by excellent public transportation connections. Join us! To apply, please share the following application documents with us through our recruitment site (\"Apply now!”) latest at 23.59pm (EET) 22 October 2026. Design Practice portfolio including maximum of six relevant projects describing your role and highlights/relevance to this call.  Please notice that the maximum size of the file is 5MB. Motivation Letter including your vision for the field TENK-compliant CV ( link to the template ) Teaching Portfolio according to Aalto guidelines ( link to the guidelines ) Please note: Aalto University’s employees should apply for the position via our internal HR system Workday (Internal Jobs) by using their existing Workday user account (not via the external webpage for open positions). If you are a student or visitor at Aalto University, please apply with your personal email address (not aalto.fi) via Aalto University open positions For more information about lecturer career, see here: Lecturer career system | Aalto University If you have questions about the role, please contact Senior University Lecturer Heidi Paavilainen heidi.paavilainen(at) aalto.fi. For questions related to the application process, please contact katju.helminen(at)aalto.fi. Want to know more about us and your future colleagues ? You can watch these videos: This is Aalto University! Aalto University – Towards a better world and Shaping a Sustainable Future . Read more about working at Aalto: https://www.aalto.fi/en/careers-at-aalto and c heck out our new virtual campus experience: https://virtualtour.aalto.fi About Finland Finland is a great place for living with or without family – it is a safe, politically stable and well-organized Nordic society. Finland is consistently ranked high in quality of life and was listed again as the happiest country in the world: World Happiness Report For more information about living in Finland: Aalto Careers for International Staff . More about Aalto University: Aalto.fi youtube.com/user/aaltouniversity linkedin.com/school/aalto-university/ www.facebook.com/aaltouniversity instagram.com/aaltouniversity To view information about Workday Accessibility, please click here . Please see more of our Open Positions here. Interested? Apply now! Updated: 11.9.2026 Published: 11.9.2026 Share URL copied! Home Open positions University Teacher or University Lecturer in Design and Manufacturing Technology Sign of Change Aalto University P.O. Box 11000 (Otakaari 1B) FI-00076 AALTO Switchboard: +358 9 47001 Follow us: Facebook LinkedIn Bluesky Instagram Youtube Snapchat Blogs Quicklinks Research and artistic outputs Library – Learning Centre Admissions Alumni Media IT services Open University Aalto University Shop Site index Latest News Events Careers Contact Campus maps Contact information Ethical channel – Whistleblowing For students Student Guide Webmail MyCourses MyStudies Sisu Together towards a better world. Support new ideas, research, work and leadership development towards a stronger Finland. Donate to Aalto University Privacy notice Cookie policy Feedback Accessibility statement Cookie settings Suomeksi Svenska English"
    },
    "https://www.aalto.fi/en/open-positions/doctoral-researcher-in-backscatter-assisted-wireless-positioning": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Backscatter-Assisted Wireless Positioning",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher in Backscatter-Assisted Wireless Positioning | Aalto University Skip to main content Sign of Change Sign of Change Donate Apply to Aalto Valitse sivuston kieli / Välj webbplatsens språk / Select site language EN FI Suomeksi SV Svenska EN English Search Log in Menu Close menu Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Admissions and studies Apply to Aalto Find a study programme How to apply Scholarships and tuition fees Bachelor's admissions (programmes in Finnish and Swedish) Bachelor’s admissions (programmes in English) Master's admissions Doctoral admissions Campus life Events for applicants Chat with students Subscribe to newsletter Contact admission services Founder School: from students to founders Lifewide Learning Exchange students Research and art About our research and art Tenure track career system Doctoral education Research and learning infrastructures Research portal research.aalto.fi Rankings Schools and departments Schools School of Arts, Design and Architecture School of Business School of Chemical Engineering School of Electrical Engineering School of Engineering School of Science Departments Accounting & Business Law Applied Physics Architecture Art and Media Bioproducts and Biosystems Built Environment Chemical and Metallurgical Engineering Chemistry and Materials Science Civil Engineering Computer Science Design Economics Electrical Engineering and Automation Electronics and Nanoengineering Film, Television and Scenography Finance Industrial Engineering and Management Information and Communications Engineering Information and Service Management Management Studies Marketing Mathematics and Systems Analysis Energy and Mechanical Engineering Neuroscience and Biomedical Engineering Other units Language Centre Library - Learning Centre Collaboration Collaborate with us For alumni Corporate collaboration Aalto networking platform Entrepreneurship and innovations Cooperation with HEI and research institutes Collaboration with cities and regions Support us News and events Highlights News Events Aalto University Magazine OurBlogs Podcasts About us About Aalto University Our strategy Sustainability Code of Conduct Aalto Handbook Campus People and contact information For the media Careers Tools and services All tools (requires login) All services Most used tools Aalto AI Assistant Abacus-accounting Abacus-planning Asio (booking.aalto.fi) Halli Marketing Cloud MOT Kielipalvelu (language service) Neo People hub Phone book PowerBI report finder Salesforce (Service platform) Tiima Webmail Webropol Workday Most used services AI in Aalto Communications services HR services IT Services Learning services Occupational health Research and innovation services Teacher's Handbook Travel services For students Sisu MyCourses MyStudies Browse all courses Safety and emergencies Emergencies Safety and security observations Cyber Security Cyber Security incident report Other Aalto Space Aalto University Shop Brand library and design system Lunch menus EN FI SV Apply to Aalto Donate Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Log in Search Open positions Doctoral Researcher in Backscatter-Assisted Wireless Positioning 11.9.2026 Application closes on 18.10.2026 Unit School of Electrical Engineering Job category Doctoral Researchers Aalto University is where science and art meet technology and business. We shape a sustainable future by making research breakthroughs in and across our disciplines, sparking the game changers of tomorrow and creating novel solutions to major global challenges. Our community is made up of 16 000 students and 5 200 employees, including 446 professors. Our campus is in Espoo, Greater Helsinki, Finland. Diversity is part of who we are, and we actively work to ensure our community’s diversity and inclusiveness. This is why we warmly encourage qualified candidates from all backgrounds to join our community. Would you like to develop new wireless positioning methods for challenging non-line-of-sight environments and validate them through real radio experiments? We are looking for a Doctoral Researcher in Backscatter-Assisted Wireless Positioning to join the Department of Information and Communications Engineering at Aalto University. The position is part of the Research Council of Finland project Backscatter Assisted Non-line-of-sight Positioning (BANLOS) . The project investigates how backscatter communications can enable and improve wireless positioning when direct line-of-sight propagation is unavailable or unreliable. As a doctoral researcher, you will work towards a doctoral degree while contributing to research at the intersection of wireless positioning, backscatter communications, statistical signal processing, and software-defined radio experimentation . Depending on your background and interests, your research may emphasize theoretical modelling and algorithms, experimental implementation, or a combination of the two. Your role and research Your main goal will be to develop and experimentally validate methods that use backscatter-assisted radio measurements to improve positioning in challenging propagation environments. The detailed research questions will be refined together with your supervisors as your doctoral research progresses. Your work may include: Developing signal models, algorithms, and performance analyses for backscatter-assisted non-line-of-sight positioning Applying detection and estimation theory to questions such as detectability, identifiability, positioning accuracy, and robustness Designing and implementing software-defined radio prototypes and measurement experiments Evaluating the proposed methods through simulations, laboratory experiments, and relevant measurement datasets Publishing your research in high-quality international journals and conferences and presenting your results to the scientific community Completing doctoral studies and developing the research skills required for a doctoral degree Participating in teaching and other academic activities of the department to a limited extent The precise balance between theoretical and experimental research can be tailored according to your background and the scientific direction of the project. Your research environment and supervision You will join the BANLOS project in the research group of Professor Riku Jäntti at Aalto University's Department of Information and Communications Engineering. The research environment brings together expertise in wireless communications, radio positioning, statistical signal processing, and experimental radio systems. You will collaborate with researchers and students at Aalto University as well as with the project's wider national and international scientific network. You will receive regular scientific supervision and support in developing the skills needed to become an independent researcher. As your doctoral work progresses, you will also be encouraged to develop your own research ideas, build scientific networks, and initiate new collaborations. What we expect from you We are looking for a motivated, curious, and collaborative candidate who enjoys tackling challenging technical problems and is interested in developing into an independent researcher. You should have: A Master's degree, or equivalent, in electrical engineering, communications engineering, signal processing, computer science, applied mathematics, or another closely related field A strong foundation in wireless communications, statistical signal processing, estimation theory, or a related area Good mathematical and analytical skills Programming skills suitable for numerical simulation, signal processing, or experimental research Good written and spoken English Motivation and ability to pursue doctoral studies and conduct long-term research The Master's degree should be completed by the start of the employment. We particularly value experience or interest in one or more of the following: Detection and estimation theory Wireless positioning and localization Backscatter or wireless communications Statistical signal processing Software-defined radio and experimental wireless systems Python, MATLAB, C/C++, GNU Radio, or comparable research tools Previous experience in all these areas is not expected. We welcome applicants whose main strengths are either theoretical or experimental, provided that they are motivated to develop the complementary skills needed for the project. Previous publication experience is not required. In the selection, we will place particular emphasis on the applicant's research potential, academic background, analytical and problem-solving skills, motivation for the research topic, and ability to conduct doctoral research. Doctoral studies at Aalto University The position is intended for a researcher pursuing a doctoral degree at the Aalto Doctoral Programme in Electrical Engineering. The selected candidate must fulfil the eligibility and admission requirements of the Doctoral Programme in Electrical Engineering. If you do not already have a doctoral study right at Aalto University, you will apply for the study right after being selected for the position. More information about the doctoral programme, eligibility requirements, and doctoral admissions is available on the Aalto University website under Aalto Doctoral Programme in Electrical Engineering . What we offer At Aalto University, you will benefit from: A fully funded doctoral researcher position and the opportunity to work towards a doctoral degree A research topic combining fundamental questions in statistical estimation with practical wireless systems and experiments An international research environment with strong expertise in wireless communications, positioning, and signal processing Close scientific supervision while gradually developing independence as a researcher Access to computing, software-defined radio, radio prototyping, and measurement resources for theoretical and experimental research Support for scientific publishing, international conference participation, research visits, professional development, and building your future research career Occupational healthcare and other employee benefits provided by Aalto University The position follows the School of Electrical Engineering's doctoral researcher employment practices. The initial employment contract is for two years, with a six-month probationary period. Following a successful mid-term review, the contract is expected to be extended for a further two years, giving a total duration of four years. The salary is determined according to the salary system of Finnish universities. The starting salary for a doctoral researcher is EUR 3,143 per month (gross) and develops as the doctoral research and studies progress. The preferred starting date is as soon as possible, but the exact date can be agreed with the selected candidate. The primary workplace is Aalto University's Otaniemi campus in Espoo, Finland. The duties of the position are carried out in Finland, with flexible working arrangements available in accordance with Aalto University practices. Ready to apply? If you would like to join us, please submit your application in English through Aalto University's online recruitment system using the \"Apply now\" link no later than October 18th, 2026 (23:59 EEST) . Applications submitted by email will not be accepted. We encourage you to apply early, as we will go through applications, and we may invite suitable candidates to interview already during the application period. All materials must be submitted in PDF format, with up to five (5) files, each no larger than 5 MB. The application materials must include: Motivation letter describing your interest in the position, relevant background, and motivation for doctoral research in the BANLOS project Curriculum vitae , including the contact details of at least two referees Copies of academic transcripts and degree certificates for your Bachelor's and Master's degrees You may also include a list of publications or other relevant research outputs if applicable , but previous publications are not required. We encourage you to explain in your motivation letter how your background relates to one or more of the project's research areas. We do not expect applicants to have prior expertise in every aspect of the project. Please note: Aalto University's employees should apply for the position via our internal HR system Workday (Internal Jobs) using their existing Workday user account, rather than through the external webpage for open positions. If you are a student or visitor at Aalto University, please apply using your personal email address rather than your aalto.fi address through Aalto University Open Positions . Further information For further information about the research topic and the doctoral researcher position, please contact Professor Riku Jäntti , riku.jantti@aalto.fi . For questions concerning the recruitment process, please contact HR Advisor, hr-elec@aalto.fi . About the Department of Information and Communications Engineering The Department of Information and Communications Engineering at Aalto University conducts high-impact research and education in communications engineering, signal processing, networking, and related digital technologies. Our international community combines rigorous theory with experimental research and close collaboration across disciplines. About Finland Finland is a great place for living with or without a family. It is a safe, politically stable, and well-organized Nordic society and consistently ranks highly in international comparisons of quality of life. For more information about living and working in Finland, see Aalto Careers for International Staff More about Aalto University: Aalto.fi youtube.com/user/aaltouniversity linkedin.com/school/aalto-university/ www.facebook.com/aaltouniversity instagram.com/aaltouniversity To view information about Workday Accessibility, please click here . Please see more of our Open Positions here. Interested? Apply now! Updated: 11.9.2026 Published: 11.9.2026 Share URL copied! Home Open positions Doctoral Researcher in Backscatter-Assisted Wireless Positioning Sign of Change Aalto University P.O. Box 11000 (Otakaari 1B) FI-00076 AALTO Switchboard: +358 9 47001 Follow us: Facebook LinkedIn Bluesky Instagram Youtube Snapchat Blogs Quicklinks Research and artistic outputs Library – Learning Centre Admissions Alumni Media IT services Open University Aalto University Shop Site index Latest News Events Careers Contact Campus maps Contact information Ethical channel – Whistleblowing For students Student Guide Webmail MyCourses MyStudies Sisu Together towards a better world. Support new ideas, research, work and leadership development towards a stronger Finland. Donate to Aalto University Privacy notice Cookie policy Feedback Accessibility statement Cookie settings Suomeksi Svenska English"
